 2481|  53.5k|            // matching an empty string to be equivalent to matching invalid
 2482|  53.5k|            // UTF-8, even though technically matching every empty string will
 2483|  53.5k|            // split the UTF-8 encoding of a single codepoint when treating a
 2484|  53.5k|            // UTF-8 encoded string as a sequence of bytes. Our defense here is
 2485|  53.5k|            // that in such a case, a codepoint should logically be treated as
 2486|  53.5k|            // the fundamental atom for matching, and thus the only valid match
 2487|  53.5k|            // points are between codepoints and not bytes.
 2488|  53.5k|            //
